1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,700
In 2013, an astronaut almost drowned.

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:06,740
Not in the ocean, not in a swimming pool.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,060
He was floating in space.

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:11,660
His name was Luca Parmitano,

5
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:14,540
and on July 16th, he was working outside the

6
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:17,100
International Space Station when he felt something

7
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:18,160
strange.

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:19,140
Water.

9
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,840
Inside his helmet.

10
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:23,560
At first, he thought his drinking bag was leaking,

11
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,480
but the water kept coming.

12
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,720
And in zero gravity, water doesn't simply fall

13
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:29,840
to the ground.

14
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,320
It began spreading around his head,

15
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:34,680
covering his ears, his eyes,

16
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,840
and eventually, his nose.

17
00:00:37,260 --> 00:00:39,700
NASA ordered him to return to the station,

18
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:41,080
but there was a problem.

19
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,680
He could barely see.

20
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:44,960
His radio communication was failing,

21
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,700
and just as he started making his way back,

22
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:49,960
the station moved into darkness.

23
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:53,580
Imagine being hundreds of kilometers above Earth,

24
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:56,460
unable to see clearly, with water covering your

25
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,280
face.

26
00:00:57,600 --> 00:01:00,000
Luca had one thing he could rely on,

27
00:01:00,040 --> 00:01:01,260
his safety tether.

28
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,760
He followed it, feeling his way back toward

29
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,720
the airlock.

30
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,520
After reaching safety, his crewmates finally

31
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,900
removed his helmet.

32
00:01:09,180 --> 00:01:11,440
Investigators later discovered that a blocked

33
00:01:11,480 --> 00:01:13,820
component in his spacesuit's cooling system

34
00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:16,580
had allowed water to enter the ventilation system.

35
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:19,640
Around one and a half liters had collected inside

36
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:20,560
his helmet.

37
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:22,820
And here's the most disturbing part,

38
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:25,560
the suit had shown warning signs during an earlier

39
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:26,680
spacewalk.

40
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:30,020
Luca survived, but he had come dangerously close

41
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:32,820
to drowning in one of the last places anyone

42
00:01:32,860 --> 00:01:33,880
would expect,

43
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,000
space.

44
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:36,760
File Two.

45
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:39,040
The Unknown File.

